const IDX=[{"title": "Renown", "url": "rules-renown.html", "text": "renown'>Renown\n A turn-based strategy game of empire building, diplomacy, and domain mastery."}, {"title": "Introduction", "url": "rules-introduction.html", "text": "Introduction\nWithin the Realm, Empires expand, specialize, confer, and when diplomacy fails\u2014battle. You will lead your humble Province to greatness. Charter settlements, pursue your economy, and negotiate your way to victory. Will your religion dominate the Realm? Will your economy grow until your wealth is undeniable? Can you build a world wonder? Can you extort your way to victory? Pick your Faction, command your Domain, and pursue your Craft in this political grand strategy, where every action you attempt can be endorsed or condemned by your allies and other players.\nGame Synopsis\nRenown is a turn-based political strategy game for 1\u20137 players (3+ preferred) set in a medieval world of competing lords. Each player controls a growing empire \u2014 settlements, armies, and pursuits \u2014 but the game\u2019s central tension isn\u2019t military. It\u2019s political.\nEvery action you want to take has to survive a vote. When you move your army, build a road, or sabotage a rival, every other player at the table gets to spend political influence to support or bury it. The strength of your relationships, the alliances you\u2019ve built, and the favors you\u2019re owed determine whether your plans succeed \u2014 not just your re"}, {"title": "Reading These Rules", "url": "rules-reading-these-rules.html", "text": "Reading These Rules\nA few conventions make every rule in this book read the same way:\n\nmay marks something optional. If a rule doesn&#x27;t say may, it&#x27;s mandatory.\ncan&#x27;t and doesn&#x27;t are hard stops, and always win over a may or a must (see Core Principle 2).\nEffects are written by when they apply: While X is always on; When X / At X happens once, at that moment; an action&#x27;s Cost / Effect / Endorsed happens when you take the action.\nChoose one: marks a set of options from which you pick exactly one.\nItalic text is reminder, example, or strategy \u2014 it explains the rule but never changes it; the plain-text rule governs.\nCapitalized terms (Army, Envoy, Standing, Pursuit, Treaty\u2026) are defined terms \u2014 look them up in the Compendium.\n"}, {"title": "Core Principles", "url": "rules-core-principles.html", "text": "Core Principles\n\nGranted Authority. Any mechanic not explicitly described doesn&#x27;t function.\n\n\nSpecific over general. A more specific rule overrides a general one.\n\n2.1 Example: Inquisitorial Palace \u2265 Established Cunning &gt; general Cunning rule.\n2.2 When two effects conflict, the one that says can&#x27;t (or doesn&#x27;t) takes precedence over one that says you may or must.\n\n\n\nPublic information. All information is public: resources, Domains, Treaties, Armies, Pursuits, and Garrisons are known to all players.\n\n\nOnce per turn, same target. A once-per-turn effect can&#x27;t be used on the same target twice in a turn.\n\n\nInnate + Mastery are cumulative.\n\n\nDamaged means inactive. A Damaged Pursuit or Infrastructure has neither its innate nor its mastery effect.\n\n\nTimer 0 resolves immediately. Any timer whose initial value is 0 or less resolves at once.\n\n\nDo as much as possible. Follow as much of an effect as you can; ignore any part you can&#x27;t carry out.\n\n\nDice.\n\n9.1 If a Roll is modified beyond 6+, it automatically fails.\n9.2 If a Roll is modified below 2+, it automatically passes.\n9.3 If modified to 1+ or 7+ but specific results trigger on a 1 or 6, you still roll the dice f"}, {"title": "The Turn", "url": "rules-the-turn.html", "text": "The Turn\nEach turn runs through five phases in order, then passes the Host and repeats:\n\nEmpire Phase \u2014 start of turn: activate Standing effects, apply the Season, increment timers, resolve Bandit Mechanics, gain Influence &amp; Envoys, collect income, and pay upkeep.\nCouncil Phase \u2014 a Council vote on a Domain; each player then performs one action of that Domain.\nEnvoy Phase \u2014 Diplomacy Envoys first, then Domain Envoys (Prowess \u2192 Cunning \u2192 Piety \u2192 Industry).\nBattle Phase \u2014 Skirmishes, Sieges, and Battles resolve.\nRest Phase \u2014 cleanup, change Season, score Renown, spend one Domain Point, pass the Host.\n\nThe Host. Each turn one player is the Host, and the starting player is the player directly clockwise from them. The role passes clockwise each Rest Phase (except in Spring). The Host runs most of that Empire Phase&#x27;s administration: collecting and distributing Trade Income, resolving Bandit Mechanics, and breaking ties (Council vote, Bandit targeting, and anything not otherwise resolvable). The Host Card carries the step-by-step detail.\nTimers\nMany actions set a Timer to a number of turns. Each Empire Phase, every active Timer ticks down by 1; when a Timer reaches 0 it resolves a"}, {"title": "Table Setup", "url": "rules-table-setup.html", "text": "Table Setup\n\nDomain Board: set Renown to 1, set each player&#x27;s Standing in each Domain to 1, set Season to Summer, and set Public Order to 0.\nGive the Host Card to the player who wants to Host first. If more than one, roll off.\nHex Map.\nTactic Decks, Equipment &amp; Retinue Cards, Pursuit Tiles, Bandit Camps, and the various tokens.\n"}, {"title": "Player Setup", "url": "rules-player-setup.html", "text": "Player Setup\n\nPick a Faction Card (optional for new players).\nEmpire Tableau.\nCollect 1 Town, 1 Village, and 1 Hamlet. Take turns placing Towns, starting with the Starting player. Then each player may place their first Village Range 4 from their Town, and their Hamlet Range 2 from their Town. Then place Outlaw Country Range 2 from their Town or Village, but not adjacent to their Hamlet.\nCollect 10,000 Gold, 2 Influence Tokens, and 1 Envoy.\nYou don&#x27;t begin the game with any Armies.\nFor the first turn, begin at the Council Phase instead of the Empire Phase.\n"}, {"title": "Action Mechanics", "url": "rules-action-mechanics.html", "text": "Action Mechanics\nenvoy'>Sending an Envoy\nEnvoys are the currency of actions: to perform an action you send an Envoy during the Envoy Phase. Sending costs 1 Envoy, and you must be able to pay the action&#x27;s cost before you send it. Declare the Domain but not the action \u2014 &quot;I&#x27;d like to send a [Domain] Envoy.&quot;\nenvoy'>Resolving an Envoy\nYour Envoy begins with Influence equal to your innate Influence in its Domain \u2014 Untested 1, Rising 2, Established 3, Sovereign 4 \u2014 plus any automatic Influence \u00b1X modifiers. (These come from your Pursuits, Infrastructure, and faction, and apply on their own; you never spend Influence for them.)\nThen, clockwise from the starting player, every other player may respond:\n\nSupport X \u2014 spend X of your Influence to raise the Envoy&#x27;s net Influence.\nOppose X \u2014 spend X of your Influence to lower it.\nAbstain \u2014 spend nothing.\n\nYou spend Influence only when you Support or Oppose; abstaining is free. You may let as much pass unopposed or unsupported as you like. You can&#x27;t vote on your own Envoy. Each player may spend up to 1 + their Standing in that Domain on a single vote (Untested 1, Rising 2, Established 3, Sovereign 4); Pursuits, Infras"}, {"title": "Seasons", "url": "rules-seasons.html", "text": "Seasons\nThe Realm cycles through four Seasons. The current Season&#x27;s effect is applied during the Empire Phase, and the Rest Phase advances the Season by one.\nSeasonNameEffectWinterFreezingAll Armies gain Speed -1; Sieges do not increment. Tax income collected.SpringPlantingNo Host, Bandit Mechanics, Trade Income, Council Phase, or Diplomacy Actions. Gain +1 Envoy. Bandit Camps Spawn.SummerCampaigningAll Armies gain Speed +2FallHarvestHusbandry Mastery Effects are doubled."}, {"title": "Influence", "url": "rules-influence.html", "text": "influence'>Influence\nEach turn, gain Influence from the following sources:\nSourceInfluence ChangeNotesEra+1/+2/+3/+4Based on the Current EraTrading Partners+1Per Trading Partner.Alliances+1Per Alliance Member.Infrastructure tier completed+1Per Infrastructure tier fully completed.Cunning Standing+1per unlocked Cunning Standing.Fully Mustered Army+1Per active Army of 25 Retinues.Condemned Envoy last turn-1Per Condemned Envoy last turn.At War-3While at War.Monuments &amp; Wonders+1Per active Monument or Wonder.Other sources+XFrom other effects like Pursuits.\n"}, {"title": "Prowess Actions", "url": "rules-prowess-actions.html", "text": "Prowess Actions\nActionCostRequiresEffect (if passes)EndorsedMoveNone\u2014Move an Army up to its Speed in Territories. Then choose one: March \u2014 move up to 2\u00d7 Speed, lose 1 Endurance, take no other action; Battle \u2014 end adjacent to a non-allied Army not in a Settlement, then begin a Battle; Lay Siege \u2014 end adjacent to an at-war Settlement, then begin a Siege; Muster \u2014 end within range 2 of your Settlements, not within range 1 of a non-ally, at an active Muster Field, then recruit up to your combined muster limit (you may swap Retinues between adjacent allied Armies and change equipment). \u2014 An Army may be the target of only one Move action per turn.; While an Army&#x27;s Battle, Siege, or Muster Timer is running, it can&#x27;t be the target of actions.; When an Army performs the Battle mode, it has Seize the Initiative in that Battle&#x27;s first Skirmish.Perform another Move action (same or a different Army).Declare WarNoneRising ProwessChoose a non-allied player you have no NAP or active truce with. You and that player are now At War, and any Trade Agreements between you end. If the target is in a Defensive Alliance, every member is now At War with you. \u2014 If you are in a Military Allianc"}, {"title": "Cunning Actions", "url": "rules-cunning-actions.html", "text": "Cunning Actions\nActionCostRequiresEffect (if passes)EndorsedIntercept Caravan2000 gold\u2014Choose a player. The next turn that player is Host, Extort their Trade Income. \u2014 This affects only a single turn&#x27;s trade income; normal income resumes afterward.Extort 2000.Foster Rebellion2000 gold\u2014Choose a player. At the next Bandit Mechanics step, place a Bandit Camp of 10 Retinues in their Outlaw Country. \u2014 If that player&#x27;s Outlaw Country has no room, expand it by one Territory and spawn there instead.Extort 2000.Raze2000 gold\u2014Choose another player&#x27;s Settlement, then choose one active Pursuit, active Infrastructure, or active Build Timer in it: that target becomes Damaged, and its effects are inactive until Repaired. A Damaged Build Timer doesn&#x27;t increment until Repaired. \u2014 A Wonder has Immune Razed and can&#x27;t be targeted.Extort 2000.Destabilize2000 gold\u2014Choose a player. In the next Extort step during Winter, Extort their Tax Income. \u2014 This affects only the next single turn&#x27;s tax income, when it&#x27;s collected.Extort 2000."}, {"title": "Piety Actions", "url": "rules-piety-actions.html", "text": "Piety Actions\nActionCostRequiresEffect (if passes)EndorsedSpread GospelDoubt 1\u2014Each non-allied player gains Doubt 1. Each allied player gains Faith 1.Gain Faith 1.Send MissionariesDoubt 1\u2014Choose a target player or Alliance. If the target is outside your Alliance, each player in it gains Doubt 2. If the target is inside your Alliance, each other allied player gains Faith 2.Gain Faith 1.TitheDoubt 1\u2014Choose a player. Extort 10% of their Treasury (round down to the nearest 100, minimum 0).Gain Faith 1.ConvertDoubt 1\u2014Choose another player&#x27;s closest non-capital Settlement; its Public Order must be \u22125 or lower. Lay Siege using only Settlement-type Siege modifiers (Settlement Size and Citadel) and set a Convert Timer. When it reaches 0, the Settlement joins your empire (see Capture). \u2014 If the target&#x27;s Public Order rises to 1 or higher before the timer reaches 0, the Convert fails and the timer is removed.Gain Faith 1.CrusadeDoubt 1Sovereign PietyDeclare War on a non-ally you have no NAP or truce with, then immediately perform a Move action with one of your Armies. \u2014 While a Crusade is active, neither player may Declare War on, Sign or End a Treaty with, Negotiate with, or Demand "}, {"title": "Industry Actions", "url": "rules-industry-actions.html", "text": "Industry Actions\nActionCostRequiresEffect (if passes)EndorsedBuild2000 gold\u2014Choose an unlocked, available Infrastructure and set a Build Timer equal to its build time. When it completes, the Infrastructure becomes active in every Settlement in your province. \u2014 You must have at least one Infrastructure from the prior tier before building the next tier.; A Wonder is built in your capital and requires all other Infrastructure to be active when the Build action is performed.Recoup 2000.Repair0 gold\u2014Choose a Damaged Pursuit or Infrastructure in a Settlement you control and set Build Timer 2. When it reaches 0, choose one: Restore \u2014 reactivate it with all effects; Demolish \u2014 remove the Pursuit tile from your Empire Tableau.Recoup 2000.Pursue2000 gold\u2014Choose an inactive Settlement Ward you control, then choose a Pursuit whose prerequisites you meet and set a Build Timer equal to its build time (usually 1). When it completes, place the Pursuit in an available Ward slot; its innate effect activates immediately, and its mastery effect activates if all mastery requirements are met. \u2014 You may have only 2 Monument Pursuits across your empire.; Power and unique Pursuits have Build Timer +1; Monu"}, {"title": "Diplomacy Actions", "url": "rules-diplomacy-actions.html", "text": "diplomacy-actions'>Diplomacy Actions\nActionCostRequiresEffect (if passes)EndorsedSign TreatyNone\u2014Ask players to agree, then choose one and both sign it: Peace Treaty \u2014 end the war, set Truce Timer 5; Trade Agreement \u2014 begin trading next turn; Non-Aggression Pact \u2014 no Declare War (ending it via End Treaty gives both Truce Timer 5); Alliance \u2014 join, form, or invite to a Defensive or Military Alliance. \u2014 When acting on behalf of an Alliance, End Treaty requires all allies to agree.; A player can&#x27;t be in more than one Alliance.Perform a Diplomacy action.NegotiateNone\u2014Propose terms to a target; they agree or refuse. Terms may include gold, Settlement ownership, Territory, signing or ending a Treaty, or promises (non-binding). \u2014 If a promise goes unfulfilled, the affected player may Declare War on the promiser.; Also used to resolve Demand Tribute and Siege surrenders.Perform a Diplomacy action.End TreatyNone\u2014Choose a target with whom you have an active Treaty and no active Truce Timer; remove that Treaty. The target doesn&#x27;t need to agree.Perform a Diplomacy action.\n\nRule: Diplomatic Mission\nIf your diplomacy envoy fails, or a treaty or agreement was not signed, you may send an"}, {"title": "Domains & Standings", "url": "rules-domains-standings.html", "text": "Domains &amp; Standings\ndomain-standings'>Domain Standings\n \tDomains are the identity of your character in Renown. As you gain Renown each turn, you gain a Domain Point, which you may spend in any of the four Domains. Each Domain Point raises your Domain value by 1 in that Domain. When your Domain value reaches three, you become Rising in that Domain \u2014 you may spend one extra Influence on another player&#x27;s Envoy of that Domain, and your Envoys gain Influence +1. This continues at a Domain value of six (Established) and again at ten (Sovereign).\nEach Standing you gain in a Domain makes you harder to oppose there and lets you oppose others more easily with your Influence. You also gain a unique effect at each Standing that makes it easier to achieve that Domain&#x27;s objectives.\n Domain Identities &amp; Traits\nDomainUntestedRising (3)Established (6)Sovereign (10)Industry\u2014Trade Secrets: Perform endorsed Pursuit.Grand Architect: May have an additional City. Perform endorsed Charter.Titan of Industry: Your capital may be chartered to a Metropolis. Perform endorsed Charter.Prowess\u2014Indomitable: Once per turn, if you have not sent a Personal Envoy, you may instead perform a Prowess ac"}, {"title": "Diplomacy & Treaties", "url": "rules-diplomacy-treaties.html", "text": "diplomacy-treaties'>Diplomacy &amp; Treaties\nTreaties &amp; Alliances\nTreatySigned ViaEraEffectPeace TreatySign TreatyAnyEnds war between the two players; sets Truce Timer 5.Trade AgreementSign TreatyAnyBegin trading (Trade Income flows from next turn). Requires bordering + active Dirt Road.Non-Aggression PactSign TreatyAnyNeither player may Declare War on the other. Ending it via End Treaty gives both a Truce Timer 5.Military AllianceSign TreatyEminenceMutual offensive pact: if a member Declares War, all members Declare War on the target next turn (and send 1 fewer envoy).Defensive AllianceSign TreatyZenithMutual defense: attacking one member puts all members at war with the attacker.\n Alliance Rules:\nNew alliance members are added by unanimous agreement.A player cannot be in more than one alliance at a time.An alliance may remove a member via End Treaty if all others agree.\nVassalization\nTo vassalize a player:\n\nControl that player&#x27;s capital Settlement while the player has no other Settlements or Armies under their Control.\n\n\nAt the end of the Rest Phase, return every Settlement you Control that was chartered by that player to that player. You become their Suzerain, and they "}, {"title": "Settlements", "url": "rules-settlements.html", "text": "Settlements\nSettlements are the primary vehicle of your Empire. They come in tiers: villages, towns, cities, and a capital Metropolis. Each tier provides tax income each turn, Settlement Wards that a Pursuit can fill, and a per-turn muster limit of Retinues. The values per tier are below:\nSettlementTaxMusterWardsReachBuildSea VariantNotesHamlet00311\u2014Husbandry pursuits only; exactly range 2 from capital; may always pursue Arable LandVillage10005111\u2014Town300010222Sea TownCity500025333PortMetropolis800025445\u2014Capital only, requires Sovereign Industry (Titan of Industry)\nSettlement Wards\nA Settlement contains 1 Settlement Ward for each of its tiers. A Village has 1 central hub, which all other Settlement Wards must be adjacent to (range 1); a Town has 2 Wards, a City has 3, and a Metropolis may have 4. The one exception is a Hamlet: it can hold only Husbandry Pursuits, but contains 3 Settlement Wards.\nChartering Settlements\nWhen chartering a new Settlement, place it at least range 4 from all other Settlements and range 2 from any Outlaw Country. You can&#x27;t charter a Settlement on mountain or water Territory. To upgrade a Village into a Sea Town, you must have a Settlement Ward adjace"}, {"title": "Infrastructure", "url": "rules-infrastructure.html", "text": "Infrastructure\n \tInfrastructure is the foundation of your Settlements. Each active Infrastructure provides an effect that applies to your entire empire and all its Settlements.\n \tExample: Wooden Walls protect all Settlements from Cunning Envoys, and a Cathedral raises your innate Faith by 1 each turn, regardless of how many Settlements you have.\n \tInfrastructure comes in 5 ascending tiers. Primitive Infrastructure builds the basic blocks of your empire. Developed Infrastructure expands and replaces some primitive Infrastructure. Sophisticated Infrastructure allows more powerful effects and helps unlock unique Monument Pursuits.\n \tLast are world Wonders. Wonders are unique Infrastructure, each built once per game, only once all other Infrastructure is built and active in your empire. They&#x27;re Edict-satisfying buildings with very powerful effects. A Wonder exists inside your capital and can&#x27;t be razed or damaged.\nThe full list of Infrastructure \u2014 their tiers, build times, upkeep, requirements, and effects:\nBuildTierUpkeepBuild TimeRequirementEffectDirt RoadsPrimitive02NoneCan Trade; If you start a Move action within Province, gain Speed +1Hitching PostPrimitive02NoneCraft +1"}, {"title": "Territory & Terrain", "url": "rules-territory-terrain.html", "text": "territory-terrain'>Territory &amp; Terrain\nTerritory is the smallest unit of land. To move from one Territory to another, you move range 1. To be within a Territory is range 0; adjacent is range 1; next to is range 2.\n \tTerritories carry modifiers by hex type (grassland, forest, tundra, wetlands, water, mountain), and are uncontrolled, contested, or controlled. Territory begins uncontrolled. By chartering Settlements you Control Territories: each Settlement&#x27;s Reach X adds every Territory within that range to your province. If another player&#x27;s Settlement Reach reaches any Territory you Control, that Territory is contested.\n \tTo border another player, your Reach must be within or adjacent to their Territory.\nTerrainEffectRaw MaterialsGrassland\u2014Arable Land, ApiaryWetlandsSpeed -1Peat Bog, ForestryTundragain StrainedQuarry, Salt WorksMountainsImpassableMineWaterMust end move after moving over 1 Water Territory (must end on land)FishmongeryForestSpeed -1Forestry, ApiaryHillGains Seize the Initiative. Where Settlements can be chartered.\u2014"}, {"title": "Public Order", "url": "rules-public-order.html", "text": "Public Order\nFaith and Doubt adjust your Public Order the moment they&#x27;re generated \u2014 each Faith raises it by 1, each Doubt lowers it by 1, applied immediately. Public Order is capped between \u22125 and 10, and your current band&#x27;s effects (below) are always active at your current value.\nFirst Doubt of the turn. Some effects (e.g. Reliquary, Episcopal Court) reduce the first Doubt you gain each turn, from any source. Because Doubt now applies immediately, this is whichever Doubt lands first in the turn \u2014 usually your innate modifiers in the Empire Phase, but it can be an opponent&#x27;s action if that resolves first. Track whether you&#x27;ve taken Doubt yet this turn; the marker resets at the start of each Empire Phase, before innate modifiers apply.\nYour innate Public Order modifiers (below) are checked once each turn during the Empire Phase and applied like any other Faith/Doubt.\nPOStateEffect-5UprisingBandit Camp spawns in your Outlaw Country-4Recession-1000 Tax Income per Settlement-3AimlessSpeed -2-2Indecisive-1 Influence-1WaveringNo effect0NeutralNo effect1FocusedNo effect2Confident+1 Influence3MotivatedSpeed +14Economic BoomTax income +500 per settlement5EurekaActivate "}, {"title": "Treasury & Upkeep", "url": "rules-treasury-upkeep.html", "text": "Treasury &amp; Upkeep\nYour Treasury is the gold you Control. Each Empire Phase you gain your Revenue (tax, trade, and Pursuit income) and pay your Upkeep (Armies, Pursuits, and Infrastructure); the net lands in your Treasury. Costs you pay during the turn come out of the same Treasury.\nTracking tip: keep three small piles \u2014 Treasury, Revenue, Upkeep. When you build something with income or upkeep, add it to the matching pile; when it&#x27;s damaged or an Army loses Retinues, subtract it. Each turn it&#x27;s just Treasury + Revenue \u2212 Upkeep, with no recounting.\nInsolvency &amp; Bankruptcy\n&gt; This is an exception path \u2014 skip it until it happens.\nYou go Insolvent the moment your Treasury can&#x27;t cover a cost in full (at Upkeep, when paying for an action, or when an effect drains your gold). Pay what you can, then cut until the books balance, in this order:\n\nDisband Retinues, one at a time, cheapest-upkeep first, until your Armies are gone.\nSet buildings inactive, highest-tier first (Monuments, then Power Pursuits, then other non-natural Pursuits).\n\nAn inactive Pursuit gives no innate or mastery effect, and anything that needed it as a prerequisite loses its mastery. An inactive p"}, {"title": "Trade & Income", "url": "rules-trade-income.html", "text": "Trade &amp; Income\nWho Can Trade &amp; Income\nWho can trade: a player needs active dirt road Infrastructure and a signed Trade Agreement to take part in trade.\nCraft X: Craft Pursuits count toward how much income your Trade Agreements generate \u2014 any effect that grants Craft +X.\nTrade income: for each active Trade Agreement, both players gain gold equal to 100 \u00d7 the Host&#x27;s Craft X.\nWhen income flows:\n\nWhen you sign a Trade Agreement: the player who did not perform the Sign Treaty action gets trade income the next time they&#x27;re Host. Afterwards, both get trade income each turn either of them is Host.\nWhen you end a Trade Agreement: the player who ended it gets trade income the next time they&#x27;re Host, then trading ceases.\n\nIncome Types\n\nTaxes: at the start of each Winter, gain tax income equal to your Settlement total, after modifiers.\nTrade: see above.\nPursuits: gain innate and active mastery effect income at the start of the income phase.\n"}, {"title": "Armies", "url": "rules-armies.html", "text": "Armies\nArmies Overview\nArmies are collections of Retinues on the realm, and are the target of Move actions. An Army holds up to 25 Retinues and up to a single piece of equipment of each type (armor, weapon, shield, and Retinue).\n \tArmies cost upkeep, paid in the Empire Phase. To find an Army&#x27;s upkeep, sum its Retinues by Retinue type cost, then subtract any upkeep modifiers.\n \tExample: Net Upkeep = Retinue Count \u00d7 (Retinue Cost \u2212 Upkeep Modifiers).\nWhile an Army has been engaged in a Battle or Lay Siege action started by another player&#x27;s Army, neither Army can be the target of any actions until that Battle or Lay Siege resolves.\nRecruiting an Army\nWhen you perform a Muster action and you&#x27;re below your Army cap, you may place an Army within (range 0) a Settlement you Control that isn&#x27;t being sieged by another player. When you do: muster Retinues up to the Settlement&#x27;s muster limit, pay the cost for the Retinue type you&#x27;re eligible to buy, choose their equipment from what you have available, and set a Muster Timer 1.\nTo muster more Retinues than the muster limit, increment the Muster Timer +1 for each additional turn&#x27;s worth of mustering. Each turn "}, {"title": "Battle Phase", "url": "rules-battle-phase.html", "text": "battle-phase'>Battle Phase\nbattle'>Begin Battle\nskirmish'>Begin Skirmish\n\nDeclare Army \u2014 declare which Army will Skirmish (if more than one is adjacent to either Army in the Battle).\n\n\nChoose a Tactic \u2014 place a face-down Tactic; reveal once the other player has too.\n\n\nDeclare equipment (if you have a tiltyard or a one-shot weapon).\n\n\nResolve Tactic modifiers \u2014 after Tactics are revealed, apply the Initiative and any other modifiers from your Tactics and weapon profile.\n\nbattle-resolves'>How a Battle Resolves\nA Battle is fought as a series of Skirmishes, run through the steps below until one side is wiped out, Routs, or successfully Falls Back. Full keyword detail is in the Compendium glossary.\nbattle-seize-the-initiative'>Begin the Battle \u2014 Seize the Initiative\nEach player rolls one D6 (+1 if they won their last Battle), re-rolling ties. The higher roller Seizes the Initiative: they become the Attacker this Battle and gain +1 Initiative in the first Skirmish; their opponent is the Defender.\nskirmish-steps'>The Skirmish Steps\n\nForm the line. Each side places up to 10 Retinues in its front line \u2014 one Strike die each \u2014 and may keep up to 5 in reserve to replace losses as they fall. An"}, {"title": "Siege Warfare", "url": "rules-siege-warfare.html", "text": "siege-warfare'>Siege Warfare\n\nWhen you Lay Siege during the Envoy Phase, track the relevant Siege Timer(s).\nWhen a Siege Timer reaches 0, resolve the Siege before the Rest Phase: negotiate, then Battle if needed, then capture or sack.\nFor the full sequence, see the steps below.\n\nsiege-timer'>Siege Timer\nA Siege Timer is the sum of the besieged Settlement&#x27;s defenses minus the attacker&#x27;s Siege effects, to a minimum of 1 (no maximum). Walls stack \u2014 a Settlement with both Wooden and Stone Walls contributes +3.\n[unknown table: siege_calculus]\nsiege'>Beginning a Siege\n\nEnd a Move action with your Army adjacent to another player&#x27;s Settlement you&#x27;re At War with.\n\n\nYour Army must stay there for the Siege Timer and can&#x27;t take other actions.\n\n\nIf you&#x27;re attacked while sieging and you Fall Back, the Siege is broken and the Siege Timer is removed from play.\n\n\nWhile a Settlement is besieged: it can&#x27;t count Pursuits toward Craft X; its Armies gain Blocked except to sally forth; timers targeting the Settlement don&#x27;t increment; and Industry actions can&#x27;t target it.\n\nsiege'>Resolving a Siege\nWhen a Siege Timer reaches 0:\n\nIf you haven&#x27;t negotiated ye"}, {"title": "Bandits", "url": "rules-bandits.html", "text": "Bandits\nOutlaw Country\nOutlaw Country is a cluster of Territory in your starting Settlement region that you can&#x27;t Control. At the start of the game, demarcate 3 Territories in your starting region, each within range 1 of at least one other Outlaw Country Territory and at least range 2 from any Settlement.\nIf that&#x27;s not possible, place them range 2 from your capital Settlement.\nbandit-camps'>Spawning Bandit Camps\nAt the start of the Bandit Mechanics step in Spring: place a Bandit Camp of 5 Bandits (Retinues) in each player&#x27;s Outlaw Country.\nNote: if an Outlaw Country is chosen to receive another Bandit Camp but there&#x27;s no room to place one, instead each existing Bandit Camp grows according to the current Era.\nbandit-camps'>Growing Bandit Camps\nA Bandit Camp becomes a Bandit Army when it reaches 25 Retinues.\nbandit-armaments-by-era'>Bandit Armaments by Era\nEraRetinues Gained per TurnFounding1Ascension2Eminence3Zenith4\nbandit-info'>Bandit Info\nBandits share the same Renown level as players. A Bandit&#x27;s Domain value is set by the size of its Bandit Camp:\n\n+1 Cunning and +1 Prowess for every multiple of 5 Bandits in the camp (e.g. 30 Retinues = 6 Cunning = Establ"}, {"title": "Quarry", "url": "type-raw-materials.html#quarry", "text": "Quarry Raw Materials +300, **Natural**; Craft +1 "}, {"title": "Salt Works", "url": "type-raw-materials.html#salt-works", "text": "Salt Works Raw Materials +300, **Natural**; Craft +1 "}, {"title": "Apiary", "url": "type-raw-materials.html#apiary", "text": "Apiary Raw Materials +300, **Natural**; Craft +1 "}, {"title": "Peat Bog", "url": "type-raw-materials.html#peat-bog", "text": "Peat Bog Raw Materials +300, **Natural**; Craft +1 "}, {"title": "Forestry", "url": "type-raw-materials.html#forestry", "text": "Forestry Raw Materials +300, **Natural**; Craft +1 "}, {"title": "Fishmongery", "url": "type-raw-materials.html#fishmongery", "text": "Fishmongery Raw Materials +300, **Natural**; Craft +1 "}, {"title": "Mine", "url": "type-raw-materials.html#mine", "text": "Mine Raw Materials +300, **Natural**; Craft +1 "}, {"title": "Arable Land", "url": "type-raw-materials.html#arable-land", "text": "Arable Land Raw Materials +300, **Natural**; Craft +1 "}, {"title": "Common Land", "url": "type-raw-materials.html#common-land", "text": "Common Land Raw Materials +500, **Natural**, **Doubt +1** "}, {"title": "Herb Garden", "url": "type-husbandry.html#herb-garden", "text": "Herb Garden Husbandry +200, **Natural** Craft +1"}, {"title": "Animal Husbandry", "url": "type-husbandry.html#animal-husbandry", "text": "Animal Husbandry Husbandry +100, **Natural**, Unlock **Crude** armor and shield. +300"}, {"title": "Saddlery", "url": "type-husbandry.html#saddlery", "text": "Saddlery Husbandry +200, **Natural** **Upkeep -200**; Speed +1"}, {"title": "Vineyard", "url": "type-husbandry.html#vineyard", "text": "Vineyard Husbandry **Natural** +600 in **Fall**"}, {"title": "Orchard", "url": "type-husbandry.html#orchard", "text": "Orchard Husbandry **Natural** +400 in **Fall**"}, {"title": "Secret Cellar", "url": "type-energy.html#secret-cellar", "text": "Secret Cellar Energy \u2014 Passed Cunning actions **Recoup 500 Gold**"}, {"title": "Pilgrimage Site", "url": "type-energy.html#pilgrimage-site", "text": "Pilgrimage Site Energy **Extort 200** every player without a Pilgrimage Site **Doubt +1** to all other players without a Pilgrimage Site"}, {"title": "Beacon Towers", "url": "type-energy.html#beacon-towers", "text": "Beacon Towers Energy \u2014 Whenever a non-allied Army ends a Move action within Province, you may immediately perform a Move action"}, {"title": "Charcoal Burner", "url": "type-energy.html#charcoal-burner", "text": "Charcoal Burner Energy +400 "}, {"title": "Mill", "url": "type-energy.html#mill", "text": "Mill Energy +300 "}, {"title": "Kiln", "url": "type-energy.html#kiln", "text": "Kiln Energy +300 "}, {"title": "Burgages", "url": "type-energy.html#burgages", "text": "Burgages Energy +200 **Faith +1**"}, {"title": "Carpentry", "url": "type-craft.html#carpentry", "text": "Carpentry Craft **Build Timer \u22121** +100; Craft+1"}, {"title": "Alchemy", "url": "type-craft.html#alchemy", "text": "Alchemy Craft +100 +200; Craft+1"}, {"title": "Masonry", "url": "type-craft.html#masonry", "text": "Masonry Craft **Build Timer \u22121** +100; Craft+1"}, {"title": "Butchery", "url": "type-craft.html#butchery", "text": "Butchery Craft +300 **Upkeep -200**; Craft+1"}, {"title": "Bakery", "url": "type-craft.html#bakery", "text": "Bakery Craft +300; Faith +1 +100; Craft +2"}, {"title": "Weavery", "url": "type-craft.html#weavery", "text": "Weavery Craft +300 +300; Craft +2"}, {"title": "Fletchery", "url": "type-craft.html#fletchery", "text": "Fletchery Craft Unlocks **Ranged Weapons** **Upkeep -200**"}, {"title": "Chandlery", "url": "type-craft.html#chandlery", "text": "Chandlery Craft +200 **Influence \u22121** to Cunning actions targeting you; Craft +1"}, {"title": "Tannery", "url": "type-craft.html#tannery", "text": "Tannery Craft Unlocks **Cast** armor & shield. **Upkeep -200**; Craft +1"}, {"title": "Joinery", "url": "type-craft.html#joinery", "text": "Joinery Craft +200, unlocks **Shields** **Upkeep -200**"}, {"title": "Furnace", "url": "type-craft.html#furnace", "text": "Furnace Craft Unlocks **Cast Weapons** +200"}, {"title": "Blacksmith", "url": "type-craft.html#blacksmith", "text": "Blacksmith Craft +200; Craft +1 Unlocks **Wrought** Tier"}, {"title": "Jewelry Foundry", "url": "type-craft.html#jewelry-foundry", "text": "Jewelry Foundry Craft +200; Craft +2 +500; **Influence +2** to Cunning Envoys targeting this player"}, {"title": "Armory", "url": "type-craft.html#armory", "text": "Armory Craft **Unlock Wrought** armor & shield **Upkeep -200**; Craft +1"}, {"title": "Master Workshop", "url": "type-craft.html#master-workshop", "text": "Master Workshop Craft **Upkeep -200**; Craft +1 Add **Serrated** to Weapons"}, {"title": "Gilded Foundry", "url": "type-craft.html#gilded-foundry", "text": "Gilded Foundry Craft Unlock **Forged** armor and shield. Tempered: Your to-Save can't be reduced beyond 10+. Craft +1"}, {"title": "Smokehouse", "url": "type-craft.html#smokehouse", "text": "Smokehouse Craft +300; Craft +1 **Upkeep -200**"}, {"title": "Workyard", "url": "type-craft.html#workyard", "text": "Workyard Craft **Doubt +1**, +400 +400"}, {"title": "Storehouse", "url": "type-craft.html#storehouse", "text": "Storehouse Craft **Doubt +2**, +600 **Build Timer \u22122**"}, {"title": "Meadery", "url": "type-craft.html#meadery", "text": "Meadery Craft **Faith +1**, +300 +200,**Speed +1** in **Winter**"}, {"title": "Winery", "url": "type-craft.html#winery", "text": "Winery Craft +400 Craft +3"}, {"title": "Cidery", "url": "type-craft.html#cidery", "text": "Cidery Craft **Faith +1**, +300 +300; Craft +1"}, {"title": "Market Square", "url": "type-craft.html#market-square", "text": "Market Square Craft Craft +2 +400"}, {"title": "Inn", "url": "type-craft.html#inn", "text": "Inn Craft **Faith +1** for trading partners with Craft 3+ **Faith +1**"}, {"title": "Spice Merchant", "url": "type-craft.html#spice-merchant", "text": "Spice Merchant Craft +300; Influence +1 to Cunning Envoys targeting you +500; Craft +2"}, {"title": "Harbor", "url": "type-craft.html#harbor", "text": "Harbor Craft +300; Craft +2 **Extort 200** per **player** without **Harbor**"}, {"title": "Merchant Quarter", "url": "type-craft.html#merchant-quarter", "text": "Merchant Quarter Craft +500 Trade Partners gain Craft +2"}, {"title": "Census Hall", "url": "type-craft.html#census-hall", "text": "Census Hall Craft **Doubt +1**; +200 +500"}, {"title": "Caravanery", "url": "type-craft.html#caravanery", "text": "Caravanery Craft **Influence -1** to **Intercept Caravan actions** targeting your **settlements** **Craft +2**; **Speed -2** to non-allied players in your Province."}, {"title": "Shipyard", "url": "type-craft.html#shipyard", "text": "Shipyard Craft Craft +1 Craft +2; Water Territory treated as Grassland for movement"}, {"title": "Money Lending", "url": "type-power.html#money-lending", "text": "Money Lending Power **Extort 500** May loan money to Trade Partners at 100 per 1000/turn interest(minimum 100); on Default: Perform **Demand Tribute**"}, {"title": "Monastery", "url": "type-power.html#monastery", "text": "Monastery Power **Influence \u22121** to Piety actions targeting you Other players can't Oppose your Piety Envoys"}, {"title": "Hospitaller", "url": "type-power.html#hospitaller", "text": "Hospitaller Power **Recover** improved by +1 Enduring: while Fatigued, your Recover rolls can't be reduced beyond 10+."}, {"title": "University", "url": "type-power.html#university", "text": "University Power May spend one additional **Influence** per Support or Oppose +1 **Influence** per Domain you are Rising"}, {"title": "College of Engineering", "url": "type-power.html#college-of-engineering", "text": "College of Engineering Power No Upkeep on **Sophisticated Infrastructure** **Build Timer \u22122**"}, {"title": "Forgery Workshop", "url": "type-power.html#forgery-workshop", "text": "Forgery Workshop Power **Extort 200** anytime a player Opposes an Envoy of yours Once/turn: attempt another Cunning Envoy targeting a different player if your Cunning Envoy Failed"}, {"title": "Levy Hall", "url": "type-power.html#levy-hall", "text": "Levy Hall Power **Upkeep -1000 while an army is range 0 of controlled settlement** **Upkeep -1000 while an army is range 0 of controlled settlement**"}, {"title": "Siege Works", "url": "type-power.html#siege-works", "text": "Siege Works Power **Siege Timer \u22121** **Siege Timer \u22121**; Sieges Increment in **Winter**"}, {"title": "Siege Camp", "url": "type-power.html#siege-camp", "text": "Siege Camp Power **Siege Timer \u22121** Armies gain **Immune Strained** during Lay Siege"}, {"title": "Citadel", "url": "type-power.html#citadel", "text": "Citadel Power **Siege Timer +1** **Siege Timer +1**, Controlled Settlements gain **Reach +1**"}, {"title": "War College", "url": "type-power.html#war-college", "text": "War College Power Gain **+2 Influence** while At War Unlocks **Sergeants** for Muster"}, {"title": "Forge", "url": "type-power.html#forge", "text": "Forge Power Craft +1 Unlocks **Forged** Tier"}, {"title": "Tiltyard", "url": "type-power.html#tiltyard", "text": "Tiltyard Power Armies may be Equipped with a second weapon (a Ranged and a Melee Weapon); the army gains **Unwieldy** Your armies have **Immune Unwieldy**. Instead, they may equip two of the same 1H Melee Weapon to gain **Dual Wield**, **Two-Handed**, and **Florentine** (while Fatigued, may Parry on a natural {FOCUSED_THR})."}, {"title": "Cipher Chamber", "url": "type-power.html#cipher-chamber", "text": "Cipher Chamber Power Once/turn when a player Sends an Envoy: that player must declare the specific Action they would Perform if the Envoy Passes (including sub-Actions). If it Passes, they must Perform that declared Action. Once/turn: select any active **Timer** you did not select last turn; increase it by 2."}, {"title": "Stable", "url": "type-civic.html#stable", "text": "Stable Civic **Speed +1** **Speed +1**; Unlocks Cavalry Weapons"}, {"title": "Coliseum", "url": "type-civic.html#coliseum", "text": "Coliseum Civic **Faith +1** while at War Unlocks **Man-at-Arms** for **Muster**"}, {"title": "Interrogation Chambers", "url": "type-civic.html#interrogation-chambers", "text": "Interrogation Chambers Civic  Cunning actions targetting this player that cause Doubt are reduced by 1, to a minimum of 0."}, {"title": "Abbey", "url": "type-civic.html#abbey", "text": "Abbey Civic Once/turn: **Influence +1** another player's Piety Envoy Morale +1."}, {"title": "Reliquary", "url": "type-civic.html#reliquary", "text": "Reliquary Civic  First **Doubt** per turn reduced by 1 (min 0)"}, {"title": "Bell Tower", "url": "type-civic.html#bell-tower", "text": "Bell Tower Civic **+1 Influence**/turn **Influence +1** to Piety actions"}, {"title": "Execution Dock", "url": "type-civic.html#execution-dock", "text": "Execution Dock Civic **Influence -1** to **Foster Rebellion actions** targeting your **settlements** **Players** who **target** you or your **settlements** with **actions** that cause **doubt** gain **Doubt +1**"}, {"title": "Jester's Court", "url": "type-civic.html#jester-s-court", "text": "Jester's Court Civic First **Oppose** on your Envoy: reduce by 1 Second **Oppose** on your Envoy: reduce by 1"}, {"title": "Embassy", "url": "type-civic.html#embassy", "text": "Embassy Civic **Influence +1** to Diplomacy Envoys Players that perform a Diplomacy action targetting you may perform another Displomacy action targetting you."}, {"title": "Granary", "url": "type-civic.html#granary", "text": "Granary Civic Upkeep -200 Armies and Garrisons gain **Endurance** while Besieged"}, {"title": "Academy", "url": "type-civic.html#academy", "text": "Academy Civic **Influence +1** to Council Envoys **Influence +1** to non-Council Envoys"}, {"title": "Courtyard", "url": "type-civic.html#courtyard", "text": "Courtyard Civic Craft +1 **Faith +1**"}, {"title": "Episcopal Court", "url": "type-civic.html#episcopal-court", "text": "Episcopal Court Civic **Faith +1** Reduce the first instance of Doubt at start of turn by 1, min 0."}, {"title": "Conditioning Field", "url": "type-civic.html#conditioning-field", "text": "Conditioning Field Civic **Faith +1** while not at War Armies gain **Nimble**"}, {"title": "Grand Tournament", "url": "type-civic.html#grand-tournament", "text": "Grand Tournament Civic **Faith +1** 3x/turn: exchange 500 gold for **1 Influence**; Armies gain **Riposte**"}, {"title": "Apothecary", "url": "type-civic.html#apothecary", "text": "Apothecary Civic +300 Gain Recover 8, or improve Recover by +1."}, {"title": "Infirmary", "url": "type-civic.html#infirmary", "text": "Infirmary Civic +200 Improve Recover by +1"}, {"title": "Supply Depot", "url": "type-civic.html#supply-depot", "text": "Supply Depot Civic **Craft +2** May **Muster** an Army in a Settlement under Siege and increment Muster Timers."}, {"title": "Artisan Workshop", "url": "type-civic.html#artisan-workshop", "text": "Artisan Workshop Civic +400 +200, **Faith +1**"}, {"title": "Trade Guild", "url": "type-civic.html#trade-guild", "text": "Trade Guild Civic No Upkeep on **Primitive Infrastructure** No Upkeep on **Developed Infrastructure**"}, {"title": "Court Artists", "url": "type-civic.html#court-artists", "text": "Court Artists Civic **Extort 500**; **Faith +1** **Extort 500**; Target of Extort gains **Faith +1**"}, {"title": "Courier Network", "url": "type-civic.html#courier-network", "text": "Courier Network Civic Once/turn: **Influence \u22121** on Target Envoy Once/turn: successfully Performed Personal Envoy can be Performed next turn; send 1 fewer Envoys next turn"}, {"title": "Toll House", "url": "type-civic.html#toll-house", "text": "Toll House Civic Once/turn when an Army ends a Move action within Province: Perform a Diplomacy action targeting that army's player **Extort 500** when non-Allied Army ends a Move action within Province"}, {"title": "Smuggler's Nook", "url": "type-secrecy.html#smuggler-s-nook", "text": "Smuggler's Nook Secrecy gain Immune Uprising (Bandit Camp Spawn at -5PO) Bandit Camps in your Outlaw Country don't target you and target other players instead randomly."}, {"title": "Black Market", "url": "type-secrecy.html#black-market", "text": "Black Market Secrecy When another player **Extorts** gold from any source: **Extort 200** per 1000 (minimum 100) from that player at the end of that resolution. When another player **Recoups** gold from any source: **Extort 200** per 1000 (minimum 100) from that player at the end of that resolution."}, {"title": "Toxicarium", "url": "type-secrecy.html#toxicarium", "text": "Toxicarium Secrecy Weapons gain **Poison** All Endorsed Cunning actions give an additional **Doubt +1** to Target"}, {"title": "Forgotten Catacombs", "url": "type-secrecy.html#forgotten-catacombs", "text": "Forgotten Catacombs Secrecy Whenever you are the target of **Extort**, reduce the Extort amount by 100 (min 100). Cunning actions against you can't be **Endorsed**"}, {"title": "Office of Works", "url": "type-monument.html#office-of-works", "text": "Office of Works Monument Settlements & allied armies inside them are not affected by 'Settlements being Besieged' restrictions. Siege Timer +2; Build Timer -2"}, {"title": "Royal Pavilion", "url": "type-monument.html#royal-pavilion", "text": "Royal Pavilion Monument Armies gain **Immune Strained** Armies gain **Drilled**"}, {"title": "Imperial Palace", "url": "type-monument.html#imperial-palace", "text": "Imperial Palace Monument Each Empire Phase, all non-allied players with a lower Prowess value gain Doubt +2. If your Envoy would fail, it passes instead."}, {"title": "Artillery Park", "url": "type-monument.html#artillery-park", "text": "Artillery Park Monument Siege Timers ignore Wooden & Stone Walls Settlements you Siege can't Sally Forth. Siege Timer \u22121."}, {"title": "Ministry of Military Strategy", "url": "type-monument.html#ministry-of-military-strategy", "text": "Ministry of Military Strategy Monument Always gains **Seize the Initiative**, and your opponent doesn't. gain Immune Tactic -1 to Strike Gain +1I & max initiative is 3; Deadly, & Cleave also trigger Focused Strikes on a natural 5."}, {"title": "Thieves' Guild", "url": "type-monument.html#thieves-guild", "text": "Thieves' Guild Monument Whenever another player performs a Cunning action, you may recoup 1000 gold **Extort 25%** of Trade Income from players who don't trade with you"}, {"title": "Senate Hall", "url": "type-monument.html#senate-hall", "text": "Senate Hall Monument **Faith +1**, gain **+1 Influence** per other player per Turn Once/turn: Before players Support or Oppose, you may auto-**Condemn** an At War Envoy OR auto-**Endorse** an Ally's Envoy"}, {"title": "Papal Palace", "url": "type-monument.html#papal-palace", "text": "Papal Palace Monument Your Piety actions that cause doubt cause an additional doubt. You no longer pay cost for Piety actions. At the start of each turn, Tithe every other player with lower Piety, resolved in the Extort step.\nOnce per turn, you may perform Spread Gospel."}, {"title": "Inquisitorial Palace", "url": "type-monument.html#inquisitorial-palace", "text": "Inquisitorial Palace Monument **Doubt +1**; Unlocks **Grand Vizier** which uses your **Public Order** instead of your **Cunning** value. You may use your **Piety Value** as **Cunning Value** for **Grand Vizier**."}, {"title": "Preceptory of the Knight's Templar", "url": "type-monument.html#preceptory-of-the-knight-s-templar", "text": "Preceptory of the Knight's Templar Monument Armies gain **Zealous**: Automatically pass the first Panic Check of every Battle. Unlocks **Knight's Templar** for Muster"}, {"title": "Manor House", "url": "type-monument.html#manor-house", "text": "Manor House Monument Gain +100 gold for each active natural specialization. Gain +100 gold for each active energy specialization."}, {"title": "Aristocratic Court", "url": "type-monument.html#aristocratic-court", "text": "Aristocratic Court Monument Each Empire Phase, Extort 1000 from each non-allied player with a lower Cunning value. Your Vote counts as 2 votes toward Domain selection during the Council Phase."}, {"title": "Studium Generale", "url": "type-monument.html#studium-generale", "text": "Studium Generale Monument +1 **Influence** per **Established** Standing May gain one **Sovereign Domain** effect without spending the Domain Points"}, {"title": "Outlaw Rookery", "url": "type-monument.html#outlaw-rookery", "text": "Outlaw Rookery Monument Both Bandit Camps & you gain Influence +1 when performing Cunning actions. Endorsed Foster Rebellion places Bandit Camps with 25 retinues instead of 10."}, {"title": "Advanced Blast Furnace", "url": "type-monument.html#advanced-blast-furnace", "text": "Advanced Blast Furnace Monument **Upkeep -500** **Crafted** Tier Unlocked; Craft +2"}, {"title": "Outrider Intercept Post", "url": "type-monument.html#outrider-intercept-post", "text": "Outrider Intercept Post Monument In the first Skirmish of every Battle, your opponent plays their Tactic Card face up before you select your own. Every Skirmish, you may force your opponent to reveal their Tactic Card they selected before you select your own."}, {"title": "Turn Sequence", "url": "turn-sequence.html", "text": "turn sequence empire council envoy battle rest phase order of play"}, {"title": "Dirt Roads", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html", "text": "Dirt Roads infrastructure Can Trade; If you start a Move action within Province, gain Speed +1"}, {"title": "Hitching Post", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html", "text": "Hitching Post infrastructure Craft +1"}, {"title": "Muster Field", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html", "text": "Muster Field infrastructure Can Muster"}, {"title": "Wooden Walls", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html", "text": "Wooden Walls infrastructure **Influence -2** to **Raze actions** from players targeting your **settlements**. **Influence -1** to Bandit **Cunning actions** targetting your **settlements**."}, {"title": "Stone Roads", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html", "text": "Stone Roads infrastructure If you start a Move action within Province, gain additional Speed +1"}, {"title": "Town Hall", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html", "text": "Town Hall infrastructure +1 Influence per turn"}, {"title": "Bridges", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html", "text": "Bridges infrastructure Armies cross Water Territory at full movement within Province; Stone Roads may be built over Water"}, {"title": "Garrison", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html", "text": "Garrison infrastructure Local Armies form (10/15/25/50 by Settlement size). All Garrisons share Equipment. Can't be targeted; may Sally Forth."}, {"title": "Stone Walls", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html", "text": "Stone Walls infrastructure **Influence -2** to **Destabilize actions** from players targeting your **settlements**. **Influence -1** to Bandit **Cunning actions** targetting your **settlements**."}, {"title": "Keep", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html", "text": "Keep infrastructure May Muster from Garrison in addition to normal Muster Limits. If so set Garrison to 0 and Muster Timer 1. Garrison returns to full when resolved."}, {"title": "Cathedral", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html", "text": "Cathedral infrastructure Faith +2"}, {"title": "Library", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html", "text": "Library infrastructure Influence +1 to Council Envoys"}, {"title": "Colossus", "url": "wonders-ref.html", "text": "Colossus wonder You may **support** your own **prowess envoys** before other **players vote**. **Armies** move **Speed +2**, **Siege Timer -2**, & gain **Immune Blunder**."}, {"title": "The Grand Exchange", "url": "wonders-ref.html", "text": "The Grand Exchange wonder Whenever you generate **Trade Income** you generate **twice as much** for yourself."}, {"title": "The Great Basilica", "url": "wonders-ref.html", "text": "The Great Basilica wonder If your **Public Order** would ever be less than 5 set it to 5 instead. Your **Settlements** gain **Reach +1**."}, {"title": "High Chancery", "url": "wonders-ref.html", "text": "High Chancery wonder Once per turn: automatically **Condemn** or **Endorse** one Envoy Sent by any other player regardless of **Net Influence** after Influence has been spent, even if it\u2019s a Council Envoy."}, {"title": "Move", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Move Prowess action Move an Army up to its Speed in Territories. Then choose one: March \u2014 move up to 2\u00d7 Speed, lose 1 Endurance, take no other action; Battle \u2014 end adjacent to a non-allied Army not in a Settlement, then begin a Battle; Lay Siege \u2014 end adjacent to an at-war Settlement, then begin a Siege; Muster \u2014 end within range 2 of your Settlements, not within range 1 of a non-ally, at an active Muster Field, then recruit up to your combined muster limit (you may swap Retinues between adjacent allied Armies and change equipment)."}, {"title": "Declare War", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Declare War Prowess action Choose a non-allied player you have no NAP or active truce with. You and that player are now At War, and any Trade Agreements between you end. If the target is in a Defensive Alliance, every member is now At War with you."}, {"title": "Demand Tribute", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Demand Tribute Prowess action Choose a non-allied player you have no NAP with, then negotiate terms. If the target agrees, sign a NAP or Alliance (the target picks among the offered terms). If the target refuses, or later fails to meet the terms, immediately Declare War on them."}, {"title": "Intercept Caravan", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Intercept Caravan Cunning action Choose a player. The next turn that player is Host, Extort their Trade Income."}, {"title": "Foster Rebellion", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Foster Rebellion Cunning action Choose a player. At the next Bandit Mechanics step, place a Bandit Camp of 10 Retinues in their Outlaw Country."}, {"title": "Raze", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Raze Cunning action Choose another player's Settlement, then choose one active Pursuit, active Infrastructure, or active Build Timer in it: that target becomes Damaged, and its effects are inactive until Repaired. A Damaged Build Timer doesn't increment until Repaired."}, {"title": "Destabilize", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Destabilize Cunning action Choose a player. In the next Extort step during Winter, Extort their Tax Income."}, {"title": "Spread Gospel", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Spread Gospel Piety action Each non-allied player gains Doubt 1. Each allied player gains Faith 1."}, {"title": "Send Missionaries", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Send Missionaries Piety action Choose a target player or Alliance. If the target is outside your Alliance, each player in it gains Doubt 2. If the target is inside your Alliance, each other allied player gains Faith 2."}, {"title": "Tithe", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Tithe Piety action Choose a player. Extort 10% of their Treasury (round down to the nearest 100, minimum 0)."}, {"title": "Convert", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Convert Piety action Choose another player's closest non-capital Settlement; its Public Order must be \u22125 or lower. Lay Siege using only Settlement-type Siege modifiers (Settlement Size and Citadel) and set a Convert Timer. When it reaches 0, the Settlement joins your empire (see Capture)."}, {"title": "Crusade", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Crusade Piety action Declare War on a non-ally you have no NAP or truce with, then immediately perform a Move action with one of your Armies."}, {"title": "Build", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Build Industry action Choose an unlocked, available Infrastructure and set a Build Timer equal to its build time. When it completes, the Infrastructure becomes active in every Settlement in your province."}, {"title": "Repair", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Repair Industry action Choose a Damaged Pursuit or Infrastructure in a Settlement you control and set Build Timer 2. When it reaches 0, choose one: Restore \u2014 reactivate it with all effects; Demolish \u2014 remove the Pursuit tile from your Empire Tableau."}, {"title": "Pursue", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Pursue Industry action Choose an inactive Settlement Ward you control, then choose a Pursuit whose prerequisites you meet and set a Build Timer equal to its build time (usually 1). When it completes, place the Pursuit in an available Ward slot; its innate effect activates immediately, and its mastery effect activates if all mastery requirements are met."}, {"title": "Charter", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Charter Industry action Choose one: Charter a new Village \u2014 on uncontrolled or in-province non-water, non-mountain Territory, range 4+ from any Settlement and range 2+ from Outlaw Country; or Expand a non-City Settlement one tier into an adjacent Territory (Village to Sea/Town, Sea/Town to Port/City, Port/City to Metropolis), adding a Ward."}, {"title": "Sign Treaty", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Sign Treaty Diplomacy action Ask players to agree, then choose one and both sign it: Peace Treaty \u2014 end the war, set Truce Timer 5; Trade Agreement \u2014 begin trading next turn; Non-Aggression Pact \u2014 no Declare War (ending it via End Treaty gives both Truce Timer 5); Alliance \u2014 join, form, or invite to a Defensive or Military Alliance."}, {"title": "Negotiate", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Negotiate Diplomacy action Propose terms to a target; they agree or refuse. Terms may include gold, Settlement ownership, Territory, signing or ending a Treaty, or promises (non-binding)."}, {"title": "End Treaty", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "End Treaty Diplomacy action Choose a target with whom you have an active Treaty and no active Truce Timer; remove that Treaty. The target doesn't need to agree."}, {"title": "Envoy Outcomes", "url": "envoy-outcomes-ref.html", "text": "envoy outcomes condemned failed passed endorsed net influence resolve domain"}, {"title": "Peace Treaty", "url": "treaties-ref.html", "text": "Peace Treaty treaty Ends war between the two players; sets Truce Timer 5."}, {"title": "Trade Agreement", "url": "treaties-ref.html", "text": "Trade Agreement treaty Begin trading (Trade Income flows from next turn). Requires bordering + active Dirt Road."}, {"title": "Non-Aggression Pact", "url": "treaties-ref.html", "text": "Non-Aggression Pact treaty Neither player may Declare War on the other. Ending it via End Treaty gives both a Truce Timer 5."}, {"title": "Military Alliance", "url": "treaties-ref.html", "text": "Military Alliance treaty Mutual offensive pact: if a member Declares War, all members Declare War on the target next turn (and send 1 fewer envoy)."}, {"title": "Defensive Alliance", "url": "treaties-ref.html", "text": "Defensive Alliance treaty Mutual defense: attacking one member puts all members at war with the attacker."}, {"title": "Sovereign Standing", "url": "edicts-ref.html", "text": "Sovereign Standing edict win Reach a Sovereign Standing (Domain value 10) in any Domain."}, {"title": "Monument", "url": "edicts-ref.html", "text": "Monument edict win Have an active Mastery Effect of a Monument pursuit."}, {"title": "Wonder", "url": "edicts-ref.html", "text": "Wonder edict win Complete a World Wonder."}, {"title": "Wealth", "url": "edicts-ref.html", "text": "Wealth edict win Generate 5,000 gold per turn for five consecutive turns, net Upkeep costs."}, {"title": "Vassalize", "url": "edicts-ref.html", "text": "Vassalize edict win Vassalize a rival player (control their capital with no other settlements/armies under them)."}, {"title": "Living Saints", "url": "edicts-ref.html", "text": "Living Saints edict win Sustain Public Order 10 (Living Saints) for five consecutive turns (Pious Timer)."}, {"title": "Last Alliance Standing", "url": "edicts-ref.html", "text": "Last Alliance Standing edict win Be the last alliance standing \u2014 the game-ending stop condition."}, {"title": "Economy Reference", "url": "economy-ref.html", "text": "upkeep costs pursuit army infrastructure tax trade 2000 gold (the envoy action; pursuit then costs per-turn upkeep by type) Per turn by type (fixed): Monument 300, Power 200, Energy 0, all others 0 retinue count x (retinue cost - Upkeep -X modifiers) Per-settlement (see INFRASTRUCTURE); Trade Guild removes Primitive/Developed, College of Engineering removes Sophisticated 2000 gold (Intercept Caravan / Foster Rebellion / Raze / Destabilize) 2000 gold (Build / Repair / Pursue / Charter) Doubt 1 (Spread Gospel / Send Missionaries / Tithe / Convert / Crusade) None (Move / Declare War / Demand Tribute) None (Sign Treaty / Negotiate / End Treaty) Extort 1000 per settlement tier; reduce settlement by 1 tier; Sack Timer 2 500 gold per settlement tier per turn (collected in Winter) 100 x host's Craft X per active Trade Agreement"}, {"title": "Grassland", "url": "terrain-ref.html", "text": "Grassland terrain \u2014"}, {"title": "Wetlands", "url": "terrain-ref.html", "text": "Wetlands terrain Speed -1"}, {"title": "Tundra", "url": "terrain-ref.html", "text": "Tundra terrain gain Strained"}, {"title": "Mountains", "url": "terrain-ref.html", "text": "Mountains terrain Impassable"}, {"title": "Water", "url": "terrain-ref.html", "text": "Water terrain Must end move after moving over 1 Water Territory (must end on land)"}, {"title": "Forest", "url": "terrain-ref.html", "text": "Forest terrain Speed -1"}, {"title": "Hill", "url": "terrain-ref.html", "text": "Hill terrain Gains Seize the Initiative. Where Settlements can be chartered."}, {"title": "Terrain & Movement", "url": "terrain-ref.html", "text": "terrain movement grassland wetland tundra mountain water forest roads bridge"}, {"title": "Bandits", "url": "bandits-ref.html", "text": "bandits outlaw country camp army growth cunning raze destabilize"}, {"title": "Timers, Influence & PO", "url": "systems-ref.html", "text": "timers influence public order modifiers faith doubt border tension"}, {"title": "Settlements", "url": "settlements-ref.html", "text": "settlements hamlet village town city metropolis tax muster wards reach"}, {"title": "Eras", "url": "eras-ref.html", "text": "eras founding ascension eminence zenith renown army cap"}, {"title": "Public Order Track", "url": "public-order-ref.html", "text": "public order faith doubt uprising living saints"}, {"title": "Domain Board", "url": "domain-board-ref.html", "text": "domain board standing indomitable grand vizier influence"}, {"title": "Seasons", "url": "seasons-ref.html", "text": "seasons winter spring summer fall"}, {"title": "Equipment", "url": "equipment-ref.html", "text": "equipment retinues weapons ranged shields armor stats"}, {"title": "Reference Tables", "url": "reference-tables.html", "text": "bandits timers influence gain trade rules build timers tier unlock standing effects"}, {"title": "Tactic Matrix", "url": "tactic-matrix-ref.html", "text": "tactic matrix scout ambush flank charge fighting defensive formation fall back initiative"}, {"title": "Escalation Campaign", "url": "escalation.html", "text": "escalation campaign combat battle mode overview"}, {"title": "Escalation Battle Rules", "url": "escalation-rules.html", "text": "escalation battle rules setup turn sequence skirmish walkthrough victory points dice"}, {"title": "Escalation Combat Pursuits", "url": "escalation-pursuits.html", "text": "escalation combat pursuits industry prowess piety cunning ranks mastery monument"}, {"title": "Combat Keywords", "url": "keywords-ref.html", "text": "keywords deadly cleave poison parry riposte"}, {"title": "Steady", "url": "glossary.html#steady", "text": "Steady Initiative cannot be reduced by Tactics."}, {"title": "Unwieldy", "url": "glossary.html#unwieldy", "text": "Unwieldy Initiative cannot be improved by Tactics."}, {"title": "Two-Handed", "url": "glossary.html#two-handed", "text": "Two-Handed Cannot use a Shield."}, {"title": "Deadly", "url": "glossary.html#deadly", "text": "Deadly On a Focused Strike: that strike's AP is set to -5, and the defender may Parry or Recover only with a Focused roll."}, {"title": "Unstoppable", "url": "glossary.html#unstoppable", "text": "Unstoppable Parried only by a Focused roll."}, {"title": "Cleave", "url": "glossary.html#cleave", "text": "Cleave On a Focused Strike: roll one extra Strike die at your modified to-Strike."}, {"title": "Poison", "url": "glossary.html#poison", "text": "Poison When the Defender receives a Strike and rolls a Focused Save, it fails; the resulting wound may only be Recovered with a Focused Recover."}, {"title": "Nimble", "url": "glossary.html#nimble", "text": "Nimble Gain +1 Initiative in the first Skirmish of each Battle."}, {"title": "Drilled", "url": "glossary.html#drilled", "text": "Drilled Does not lose Endurance in the first Skirmish of each Battle."}, {"title": "Destroy Shield", "url": "glossary.html#destroy-shield", "text": "Destroy Shield On a Focused Strike: the target loses its Shield attributes for the rest of the Battle."}, {"title": "Blunder", "url": "glossary.html#blunder", "text": "Blunder At Initiative -2 or lower, your to-Strike is set to 10+, before other negative modifiers."}, {"title": "One-Shot", "url": "glossary.html#one-shot", "text": "One-Shot May only be Equipped in the first Skirmish of a Battle. Requires a Tiltyard."}, {"title": "Parry", "url": "glossary.html#parry", "text": "Parry While not Fatigued, roll a D10 to attempt to Parry a Strike before the Save. On a 8+, the Strike is Parried."}, {"title": "Riposte", "url": "glossary.html#riposte", "text": "Riposte While not Fatigued, if you Focused a Parry against a Melee Weapon's Strike, you Riposte: your opponent immediately takes a Strike from your melee weapon. You can Riposte a Riposte."}, {"title": "Recover", "url": "glossary.html#recover", "text": "Recover While not Fatigued, if a to-Save roll fails, roll a D10: a result of X+ Recovers the retinue."}, {"title": "Serrated", "url": "glossary.html#serrated", "text": "Serrated A cumulative -2 penalty to the defender's Recover roll."}, {"title": "Tempered", "url": "glossary.html#tempered", "text": "Tempered A Focused Save succeeds, regardless of AP."}, {"title": "Fatigue Token", "url": "glossary.html#fatigue-token", "text": "Fatigue Token Each token is -2 to your Strike (to a maximum of 10+) and Morale -2 (uncapped); if your modified Morale is ever 11+, your army Routs. Tokens stack. While Fatigued, retinues cannot Parry or Recover."}, {"title": "Shielded", "url": "glossary.html#shielded", "text": "Shielded A cumulative -1 penalty to the Strike roll (to a maximum of 10+). Sources: a shield's -1 to Strike."}, {"title": "Negate Tempered", "url": "glossary.html#negate-tempered", "text": "Negate Tempered Ignores Tempered: this weapon's AP can reduce the target's Save past 10+ (to auto-fail), defeating the Tempered floor."}, {"title": "Negate Riposte", "url": "glossary.html#negate-riposte", "text": "Negate Riposte The target's Parry can never Riposte this weapon's Strikes (a natural 10 Parry still cancels the Strike, but no counter-Strike follows)."}, {"title": "Dual Wield", "url": "glossary.html#dual-wield", "text": "Dual Wield A failed Strike is rerolled once; the rerolled Strike can be Focused. Dual Wield confers Two-Handed. You cannot reroll successful Strikes."}, {"title": "Florentine", "url": "glossary.html#florentine", "text": "Florentine Only active while Dual Wielding. Even while Fatigued, a Focused Parry succeeds. This alone does not enable Riposte while Fatigued."}, {"title": "Immune [keyword]", "url": "glossary.html#immune-keyword", "text": "Immune [keyword] Cancels that keyword as it applies to you (e.g. Immune Unwieldy, Strain, Destroy Shield)."}, {"title": "AP", "url": "glossary.html#ap", "text": "AP Armor Penetration \u2014 a weapon's (negative) modifier to the defender's Save roll; the more negative, the harder to save."}, {"title": "Blocked", "url": "glossary.html#blocked", "text": "Blocked -1 Initiative in the first Skirmish (negated by Immune Blocked)."}, {"title": "Strained", "url": "glossary.html#strained", "text": "Strained -1 Initiative every Skirmish (negated by Immune Strain). Does not gain Endurance in the Empire Phase."}, {"title": "Seize the Initiative", "url": "glossary.html#seize-the-initiative", "text": "Seize the Initiative Won by the roll-off at the start of the Battle \u2014 the winner of their last Battle adds +1 to the roll. You become the Attacker and gain +1 Initiative in the first Skirmish. Some Tactics and the Ministry monument also grant it."}, {"title": "Attacker / Defender", "url": "glossary.html#attacker-defender", "text": "Attacker / Defender Set by the roll-off. Each Skirmish the Attacker declares equipment first; the Defender then responds."}, {"title": "Battle", "url": "glossary.html#battle", "text": "Battle One fight between two players, resolved as a series of Skirmishes until a side is wiped out, Routs, or Falls Back."}, {"title": "Skirmish", "url": "glossary.html#skirmish", "text": "Skirmish One round of a Battle, run through the numbered Battle steps; a Battle repeats Skirmishes until it ends."}, {"title": "Casualty", "url": "glossary.html#casualty", "text": "Casualty A retinue removed from the field \u2014 from an unsaved Strike or a failed Panic or Break check."}, {"title": "Field", "url": "glossary.html#field", "text": "Field Your retinues in play \u2014 front line (up to 10) plus reserve (up to 5). Casualties leave the field at once, lowering its count."}, {"title": "Endurance", "url": "glossary.html#endurance", "text": "Endurance A side's stamina. Each side that fights loses 1 per Skirmish; at 0 it becomes Fatigued."}, {"title": "Fatigued", "url": "glossary.html#fatigued", "text": "Fatigued A side at 0 Endurance. Each Skirmish its field takes a Break check, then it gains a Fatigue token. Fatigued Armies cannot Parry, Riposte, or Recover"}, {"title": "Break check", "url": "glossary.html#break-check", "text": "Break check Taken by each Fatigued side's field every Skirmish, just before it gains its Fatigue token. Roll Morale (up to 5 dice, modified by Fatigue tokens); failures are casualties, but a Break check never triggers a Panic check. Unbreakable auto-passes."}, {"title": "Panic check", "url": "glossary.html#panic-check", "text": "Panic check Taken at most once per Skirmish by a side that suffered more than 5 casualties in that Skirmish, after it Strikes back. Roll Morale (up to 5 dice); Immune Panic auto-passes."}, {"title": "Morale", "url": "glossary.html#morale", "text": "Morale How steady a retinue is when tested (lower is steadier; see the retinue table). Break and Panic checks roll it: a D10 per retinue in the field, up to 5 dice, each must meet its modified value; failures are casualties. If the modified value is ever 11+, the army Routs."}, {"title": "Rout", "url": "glossary.html#rout", "text": "Rout The army breaks and leaves the Battle (you lose it). Whenever an army's modified Morale value reaches 7 or more, it Routs automatically."}, {"title": "Fall Back", "url": "glossary.html#fall-back", "text": "Fall Back A controlled retreat that ends the Battle with at least one retinue left \u2014 a partial success."}, {"title": "Strike", "url": "glossary.html#strike", "text": "Strike A landed hit. Roll a D10, apply modifiers to the roll, and Strike on a result >= the to-Strike number. The target may then Parry, Save, and Recover."}, {"title": "to-Strike number", "url": "glossary.html#to-strike-number", "text": "to-Strike number The D10 result a retinue needs to Strike (see the retinue table; lower is better). Bonuses add to the roll; penalties and Fatigue tokens subtract."}, {"title": "Save", "url": "glossary.html#save", "text": "Save The defender's roll to avoid a casualty: roll a D10, add the weapon's AP (a negative) and the shield's Save bonus (a positive); the hit is saved on a result >= the armor value."}, {"title": "Natural roll", "url": "glossary.html#natural-roll", "text": "Natural roll The number on the die before any modifiers. Modifiers never change what counts as 'natural'."}, {"title": "Initiative", "url": "glossary.html#initiative", "text": "Initiative Decides who Strikes first each Skirmish (higher first). Runs -2 to +2 (Ministry can raise the maximum to +3). At -2 or lower you Blunder."}, {"title": "Tactic", "url": "glossary.html#tactic", "text": "Tactic A choice both players make secretly and reveal together each Skirmish; it can shift Initiative, Strike, and Save rolls."}, {"title": "Dual-equip", "url": "glossary.html#dual-equip", "text": "Dual-equip Carry two weapons at once (e.g. melee + ranged). Granted by the Tiltyard, which also gives Unwieldy until its mastery removes it."}, {"title": "Edict", "url": "glossary.html#edict", "text": "Edict A scoring achievement / win path: reach a Sovereign Standing, complete a Monument, or fulfill a victory condition (Wonder, wealth, Vassalize, Living Saints, Last Standing)."}, {"title": "Monument", "url": "glossary.html#monument", "text": "Monument A Domain's capstone Pursuit. Completing one scores its Edict and grants a powerful effect."}, {"title": "Faith X", "url": "glossary.html#faith-x", "text": "Faith X Gain X Faith: each Faith raises your Public Order track by 1 when resolved."}, {"title": "Doubt X", "url": "glossary.html#doubt-x", "text": "Doubt X Gain X Doubt: each Doubt lowers your Public Order track by 1 when resolved."}, {"title": "Extort X", "url": "glossary.html#extort-x", "text": "Extort X Take X from the stated source: the gold goes to you instead of its owner."}, {"title": "Recoup", "url": "glossary.html#recoup", "text": "Recoup Regain the stated cost in gold after paying it."}, {"title": "Speed", "url": "glossary.html#speed", "text": "Speed An Army's movement allowance in Territories per Move action. Base Speed value of an army is Speed 2"}, {"title": "Influence", "url": "glossary.html#influence", "text": "Influence The political currency of voting. Spend it to Support or Oppose Envoys. You gain it each turn from your Era, innate modifiers (trade partners, alliances, war), Pursuits, and Infrastructure."}, {"title": "Influence X", "url": "glossary.html#influence-x", "text": "Influence X An automatic +X (or -X) to an Envoy's net Influence from a Pursuit, Infrastructure, or Faction."}, {"title": "Envoy", "url": "glossary.html#envoy", "text": "Envoy The currency of actions: send an Envoy to perform an action during the Envoy Phase. Council Envoys act on the voted Domain; Personal Envoys are sent by Era progression."}, {"title": "Vote", "url": "glossary.html#vote", "text": "Vote On each Envoy, every player in clockwise order from the starting player must Support, Oppose, or Abstain."}, {"title": "Support X", "url": "glossary.html#support-x", "text": "Support X Spend X Influence to increase an Envoy's net Influence."}, {"title": "Oppose X", "url": "glossary.html#oppose-x", "text": "Oppose X Spend X Influence to decrease an Envoy's net Influence."}, {"title": "Abstain", "url": "glossary.html#abstain", "text": "Abstain Decline to spend Influence on a vote."}, {"title": "Net Influence", "url": "glossary.html#net-influence", "text": "Net Influence The sum of an Envoy's starting Influence (1+ by Standing) and all Support, Oppose, and Influence X. The total sets the outcome: -3 or less Condemned, 0 or less Failed (gain Doubt +1), 1+ passes."}, {"title": "Endorsed", "url": "glossary.html#endorsed", "text": "Endorsed An Envoy that passes with 3+ net Influence, triggering its endorsed effect (and a Domain's Rising/Established/Sovereign endorsement)."}, {"title": "Condemned", "url": "glossary.html#condemned", "text": "Condemned An Envoy whose net Influence is -3 or less: it fails and you resolve that Domain's Condemn effect."}, {"title": "Council Phase", "url": "glossary.html#council-phase", "text": "Council Phase Before Personal Envoys, all players vote on a Domain (clockwise; Host breaks ties). Each then sends a free Council Envoy of that Domain. Council Envoys auto-Abstain and their net Influence cannot drop below 1."}, {"title": "Council Envoy", "url": "glossary.html#council-envoy", "text": "Council Envoy A free Envoy resolved in the Council Phase on the voted Domain; auto-Abstained, net Influence floored at 1."}, {"title": "Personal Envoy", "url": "glossary.html#personal-envoy", "text": "Personal Envoy An Envoy you send in the Envoy Phase to perform an action; count and reach scale with Era."}, {"title": "Envoy Outcome", "url": "glossary.html#envoy-outcome", "text": "Envoy Outcome How a Sent Envoy resolves, by Net Influence: Condemned (<= -3), Failed (-3 < Net <= 0, gain Doubt 1), Passed (>= 1), Endorsed (>= 3). The per-domain effect at each band is given by the Envoy Outcome Table; an action's own endorsed bonus overrides the domain default."}, {"title": "Charter", "url": "glossary.html#charter", "text": "Charter Found or upgrade a Settlement (Industry action)."}, {"title": "Muster", "url": "glossary.html#muster", "text": "Muster Raise retinues into an Army, up to a Settlement's muster limit (Industry/Prowess)."}, {"title": "Pursue", "url": "glossary.html#pursue", "text": "Pursue Build a Pursuit, spending its purchase cost and a Settlement ward (Industry)."}, {"title": "Build", "url": "glossary.html#build", "text": "Build Construct Infrastructure (Industry action)."}, {"title": "Repair", "url": "glossary.html#repair", "text": "Repair Restore damaged Infrastructure or Settlements (Industry)."}, {"title": "Move", "url": "glossary.html#move", "text": "Move Advance an Army up to its Speed in Territories (Prowess)."}, {"title": "Demand Tribute", "url": "glossary.html#demand-tribute", "text": "Demand Tribute Coerce gold or concessions from another player (Prowess)."}, {"title": "Diplomacy", "url": "glossary.html#diplomacy", "text": "Diplomacy Free Envoy actions for forming and ending Treaties and Trade Agreements; resolved before Domain Envoys."}, {"title": "Treaty", "url": "glossary.html#treaty", "text": "Treaty A standing agreement between players (e.g. Trade Agreement, Non-Aggression, Alliance) signed via Diplomacy."}, {"title": "Alliance", "url": "glossary.html#alliance", "text": "Alliance A Treaty binding players to mutual support; Military and Defensive Alliances unlock by Era."}, {"title": "Vassal", "url": "glossary.html#vassal", "text": "Vassal A player subordinated via Vassalization: their chartered settlements return to them, they mirror the Suzerain's Treaties, count as allied to the Suzerain, and cannot perform or be targeted by Diplomacy actions."}, {"title": "Suzerain", "url": "glossary.html#suzerain", "text": "Suzerain The player who has Vassalized another; the vassal mirrors their Treaties."}, {"title": "Renown", "url": "glossary.html#renown", "text": "Renown The shared progress track. Gain 1 per Rest Phase; thresholds raise your Era (Ascension 8, Eminence 18, Zenith 30)."}, {"title": "Domain", "url": "glossary.html#domain", "text": "Domain One of the four identities \u2014 Industry, Prowess, Cunning, Piety \u2014 raised by spending Domain points. Values 3/6/10 = Rising/Established/Sovereign Standing."}, {"title": "Domain Point", "url": "glossary.html#domain-point", "text": "Domain Point Gain 1 per Rest Phase; spend to raise a Domain value by 1."}, {"title": "Standing", "url": "glossary.html#standing", "text": "Standing Your tier in a Domain: Untested, Rising (3), Established (6), Sovereign (10). Sets max Influence per vote (1/2/3/4) and unlocks Domain effects."}, {"title": "Public Order", "url": "glossary.html#public-order", "text": "Public Order A track from -5 to 10, adjusted each turn by Faith minus Doubt; its band applies cumulative effects (see the Public Order table)."}, {"title": "Reach", "url": "glossary.html#reach", "text": "Reach How far a Settlement projects control, in Territories (by tier). Calculated like Range X"}, {"title": "Bandit", "url": "glossary.html#bandit", "text": "Bandit Neutral hostile force; Bandit Camps spawn in Outlaw Country and on low Public Order."}, {"title": "Outlaw Country", "url": "glossary.html#outlaw-country", "text": "Outlaw Country Uncontrollable territories in your starting region where Bandit Camps spawn, starting at 3 and expanding if there is no room to place new Bandit Camps."}, {"title": "Siege", "url": "glossary.html#siege", "text": "Siege Sieging a Settlement with an Army to capture it; does not increment in Winter."}, {"title": "Border", "url": "glossary.html#border", "text": "Border Your Settlement's Reach is Range 1 or within Reach of another Player's Reach."}, {"title": "Province", "url": "glossary.html#province", "text": "Province The collection of Contested Territory and Controlled Territory by your Settlement's Reach."}, {"title": "Region", "url": "glossary.html#region", "text": "Region A collection of Territories of the same Type."}, {"title": "Realm", "url": "glossary.html#realm", "text": "Realm The total collection of Regions."}, {"title": "Territory", "url": "glossary.html#territory", "text": "Territory 1 Hex."}, {"title": "Contested", "url": "glossary.html#contested", "text": "Contested Territory that is within Reach of more than one player's settlement(s). Considered Controlled by all Players that have a Settlement within Reach."}, {"title": "Controlled", "url": "glossary.html#controlled", "text": "Controlled Territory that is within Reach of a single Player's Settlement(s)."}, {"title": "Uncontrolled", "url": "glossary.html#uncontrolled", "text": "Uncontrolled Territory that is not within Reach of any Player Settlement."}, {"title": "Adjacent", "url": "glossary.html#adjacent", "text": "Adjacent Range 1."}, {"title": "Next to", "url": "glossary.html#next-to", "text": "Next to Range 2."}, {"title": "Within", "url": "glossary.html#within", "text": "Within Range 0."}, {"title": "Range X", "url": "glossary.html#range-x", "text": "Range X The amount of Territories you must move in order to get from your current position to the specific Territory."}, {"title": "Reach X", "url": "glossary.html#reach-x", "text": "Reach X The Range X characteristic which determines what Territories you Control and are in your Province."}, {"title": "Host", "url": "glossary.html#host", "text": "Host The turn's starting player, who holds the Host Card. The role passes clockwise each Rest Phase (there is no Host in Spring). The Host collects and distributes Trade Income, resolves Bandit Mechanics, and breaks ties (Council vote, bandit targeting, and any tie not otherwise resolved)."}, {"title": "Send an Envoy", "url": "glossary.html#send-an-envoy", "text": "Send an Envoy Declare a Domain, spend 1 Envoy."}, {"title": "Perform", "url": "glossary.html#perform", "text": "Perform When you Perform an action, immediately do the description of the action. Pay the action's normal Cost."}, {"title": "Resolve", "url": "glossary.html#resolve", "text": "Resolve Attempt to Perform an action."}, {"title": "Cost / Pay", "url": "glossary.html#cost-pay", "text": "Cost / Pay Cost to perform an action, usually in Gold or Doubt."}, {"title": "Fail", "url": "glossary.html#fail", "text": "Fail An unsuccessful to Hit or to Save."}, {"title": "Failed", "url": "glossary.html#failed", "text": "Failed Net Influence 0 or less."}, {"title": "Passed", "url": "glossary.html#passed", "text": "Passed Net Influence 1 or more."}, {"title": "Focused", "url": "glossary.html#focused", "text": "Focused A natural 10, before modifiers."}, {"title": "Sally Forth", "url": "glossary.html#sally-forth", "text": "Sally Forth While a settlement you control is besieged and you have an army inside it, you may Sally Forth: Battle in the Battle Phase without performing an action."}, {"title": "War Weariness", "url": "glossary.html#war-weariness", "text": "War Weariness gain Doubt 1 for each consecutive Battle you lose in the Empire Phase."}, {"title": "Ward", "url": "glossary.html#ward", "text": "Ward A slot in a Settlement that holds one Pursuit; a Settlement has one Ward per tier (a Hamlet has 3 Husbandry Wards)."}, {"title": "Efficient X", "url": "glossary.html#efficient-x", "text": "Efficient X While this Pursuit occupies the same Settlement Ward as X (the Raw Material or Pursuit named on its tile), it uses no ward of its own \u2014 the two share one ward. Placed anywhere else, it fills a ward normally. (Core Principle 14.) Note: Two Pursuits that are Efficient with the same Pursuit cannot share a Ward with each other."}, {"title": "Map Generator", "url": "maps.html", "text": "map generator procedural board terrain hex seed rivers lakes resources start map"}];const q=document.getElementById('q'),box=document.getElementById('results');let sel=-1,cur=[];
q.addEventListener('input',()=>{const v=q.value.toLowerCase().trim();sel=-1;if(v.length<2){box.style.display='none';return;}
cur=IDX.map(d=>{const t=d.title.toLowerCase(),x=d.text.toLowerCase();let s=0;if(t===v)s=100;else if(t.startsWith(v))s=60;else if(t.includes(v))s=40;else if(x.includes(v))s=15;return{d,s};}).filter(o=>o.s>0).sort((a,b)=>b.s-a.s).slice(0,14);
if(!cur.length){box.innerHTML='<a><span class=s>No matches</span></a>';box.style.display='block';return;}
box.innerHTML=cur.map((o,i)=>`<a href="${o.d.url}" data-i="${i}"><span class="t">${o.d.title}</span> <span class="s">${o.d.text.slice(0,80).replace(/</g,'&lt;')}…</span></a>`).join('');box.style.display='block';});
q.addEventListener('keydown',e=>{const a=box.querySelectorAll('a');if(e.key==='ArrowDown')sel=Math.min(sel+1,a.length-1);else if(e.key==='ArrowUp')sel=Math.max(sel-1,0);else if(e.key==='Enter'&&cur.length){location.href=cur[Math.max(sel,0)].d.url;return;}else return;a.forEach((el,i)=>el.classList.toggle('sel',i===sel));e.preventDefault();});
document.addEventListener('click',e=>{if(e.target!==q)box.style.display='none';});